{"timestamp":"2026-09-29T11:19:56.818Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0ece4-8e92-72e3-8c1f-cb0845a66634","call_id":"call_R4tqIZoQSXUFfH3tUVOm7haw","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"0cb1b9\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000014848,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3284,\"output\":\"# TieredServe CD3 RAW ↔ CSR: bounded Nsight + explicit NVTX labels\\n\\nReference: `Sys-KU/TieredServe`, commit\\n`fe133f99b22a8d5548f135de39e92f898a73b6cb` (2026-09-29).\\n\\nThis patch is for **CD3 weights in both cases, RAW KV vs original CSR KV**.\\nIt does not switch CSR to hybrid/Page16/pipeline. It does not change compression,\\ncopy descriptors, cache placement, CUDA stream assignments, scheduling, or the\\nexisting GPU dependency events. It changes Python/shell instrumentation only;\\nthere is no C++ extension or installed-vLLM rebuild in this patch.\\n\\n## Apply\\n\\nPut the ZIP in the repository root and run:\\n\\n```bash\\nunzip -q tieredserve_nsys_csr_patch_fe133f9.zip -d /tmp/tieredserve_csr_nsys_v2\\n.venv/bin/python -m pip install nvtx\\n\\nPATCH=/tmp/tieredserve_csr_nsys_v2/tieredserve_nsys_csr_patch\\n.venv/bin/python \\\"$PATCH/apply_patch.py\\\" --repo \\\"$PWD\\\" --check &&\\n.venv/bin/python \\\"$PATCH/apply_patch.py\\\" --repo \\\"$PWD\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThe installer reads the **local worktree**, matches source anchors/function\\nnames, constructs changes in a temporary directory, and checks Python and Bash\\nsyntax before writing. It does not run Git checkout/reset/pull or alter branches.\\nOriginal files, the exact applied unified diff, and SHA-256 identities are saved\\nunder `.nsys_patch_backups/<timestamp>/`.\\n\\n### Already applied the older aaa16a3 ZIP?\\n\\nIf its `.nsys_patch_backups/<timestamp>/identity.json` and `applied.patch` remain,\\nthe installer first reverses those exact old hunks **in the temporary copy** and\\nthen applies this revision. Unrelated changes outside those hunks are retained.\\nIt refuses ambiguous reverse patches or modified old helper files, without\\nchanging the repository. Do not apply the older ZIP over this patch afterward.\\n\\nA GitHub commit cannot reveal the server's uncommitted changes. The local anchor\\ncheck is intentional: an unexpected source layout is an error, not an excuse to\\nreplace a whole file with an older version.\\n\\n## Run: exactly the requested six cells\\n\\n```bash\\nbash scripts/serving/run_csr_raw_compare.sh profile --dry-run\\nbash scripts/serving/run_csr_raw_compare.sh profile\\n```\\n\\nPreset:\\n\\n- Weight codec CD3, fused MM, base rows 16 for both RAW and CSR.\\n- KV `raw,kvcomp`, with `--cd3-kv-storage csr`.\\n- Chunk 8192; request rates 1.0, 1.2, 1.4; max_num_seqs 128.\\n- 1200 requests; first/last 100 excluded by the existing client metrics.\\n- Explicit client seed 0 in both profile and perf runs.\\n- Trigger before yielding request **400 in offered/input order**, not completion\\n  order. Capture begins at the next actual model-forward boundary in the worker.\\n- 2 GUARD_IN + **32 MEASURE** + 2 GUARD_OUT model forwards.\\n\\nThe request generator and its interarrival waits remain the installed vLLM\\nclient's implementation. The trigger wrapper does not wait for server acceptance\\nor completion and does not impose a batch size. Equal request ordinal is equal\\ninput progress, **not equal active batch/context/KV state**.\\n\\nChange the window without changing source, for example:\\n\\n```bash\\nbash scripts/serving/run_csr_raw_compare.sh profile \\\\\\n  --nsys-start-request 800 --nsys-forwards 32\\n```\\n\\nDo not add `--breakdown`, `--kv-byte-metrics`, `--cd3-cpu-profile`, or `--smoke`\\nto the profile preset. The suite rejects those combinations.\\n\\nFor canonical TPOT/attainment comparison, run without the profiler:\\n\\n```bash\\nbash scripts/serving/run_csr_raw_compare.sh perf\\n```\\n\\n`perf` does not enable the new label wrappers, byte collector, request trigger,\\nor Nsight. Profile-run client TPOT/attainment is explicitly **not** marked as a\\ncanonical performance result. Nsight graph-node tracing and the diagnostic\\nPython scopes can affect runtime even for a short window.\\n\\n## What is captured, and when\\n\\nThe profile mode uses CUDA + NVTX, no statistical CPU sampling or OS context\\nswitch collection. It filters NVTX to the `TieredServe` domain instead of showing\\nlong, ambiguous legacy breakdown messages.\\n\\nThe CLI selects `node:nvtx-precapture` when local `nsys profile --help` advertises\\nit, otherwise `node`. The precapture mode is needed to associate internal\\nprojection annotations from graph construction with later replay. On an older\\nNsight version, actual kernel records and graph-piece labels remain, but internal\\nprojection-label projection is not guaranteed. An unsupported driver/collector\\ncombination may still require `--nsys-graph-mode node` on that server.\\n\\nThe worker calls cudaProfilerStart/Stop. `--capture-range-end=stop` ends collection,\\nnot the serving workload. Two trailing guards precede one final GPU synchronize,\\nlabelled **EXCLUDE.EndOfCapture.GPU_DRAIN**. There is no new synchronization in a\\nMEASURE forward, no new timing CUDA Event, and no pre-capture pipeline drain.\\n\\nScoped byte accounting creates no CSV at startup. It is inactive outside the\\ncapture. Per-forward/per-layer scalar counters are accumulated in RAM, then JSON\\nand CSV files are written **after cudaProfilerStop**. The profiler itself still\\nhas its own capture buffers and output; this is not an assertion of zero I/O or\\nzero instrumentation overhead.\\n\\n## NVTX vocabulary: host work vs GPU enqueue is explicit\\n\\nAll NVTX ranges represent **host-side code or enqueue regions**. They are not\\nGPU busy-time measurements. GPU projection can cover idle gaps between associated\\nactivities. Read actual CUDA memcpy/kernel records for busy time.\\n\\n| Label example | Exact meaning |\\n|---|---|\\n| `FWD.MEASURE f=… DECODE B=… KV=CSR` | Selected real model forward. DECODE follows current max_query_len==1 classification. |\\n| `GRAPH.ENQUEUE G037 [L036.O+GateUp+Down -> L037.QKV]` | CPU submits a graph spanning two layers. G037 is not all of L037. |\\n| `EAGER_PIECE.ENQUEUE …` | Corresponding compiled piece executes without graph replay. |\\n| `ATTENTION.ENQUEUE_REGION L037` | CPU region between graph wrappers containing eager attention submission. |\\n| `PROJECTION.WeightWait+Compute.ENQUEUE L037 QKV` | Projection implementation, including its existing weight-ready wait and fused/fallback compute submission; also labelled during graph construction. |\\n| `WEIGHT.Materialize.ENQUEUE L037 GateUp` | Weight materialization/setup/submission. It can include decomp, not just H2D. |\\n| `KV.RAW.H2D.Prepare+ENQUEUE L037` | Raw host-to-device KV path, including the raw fallback in prefill/mixed CSR batches. |\\n| `CPU.KV.Plan.REUSE L037` | Instant marker: cached plan selected. Not a range measuring a new build. |\\n| `CPU.KV.Plan.REBUILD L037` | Instant marker: this invocation requires rebuilding. |\\n| `CPU.KV.CSR.Plan.BUILD L037` | Actual plan-construction CPU function scope. |\\n| `KV.CSR.H2D+Decode.ENQUEUE L037` | Existing CSR native submit function queues both transfers and decode. **No CPU decompression is implied.** |\\n| `GPU_WAIT.KV_READY.ENQUEUE L037` | CPU registers the existing GPU wait_event. Range length is NOT GPU wait time. |\\n| `KV.D2H.Prepare+ENQUEUE L037` | KV offload setup and device-to-host submission path. |\\n| `CPU.KV.Encode.JOB L037` | CPU encode worker job, which can include a D2H-completion wait. |\\n| `CPU.KV.Encode.WaitForD2H` | Actual CPU wait for the source D2H event in the encode path. |\\n| `CPU.KV.Encode.WaitAndPublish L037` | CPU joins/publishes the newly compressed data. |\\n| `CPU.KV.Free.CALLBACK` | Existing free callback, also visible between model forwards in the same process. |\\n| `CPU.KV.CSR.Free.BATCH` / `…Free.LAYER L037` | CSR retirement functions, not GPU work. |\\n\\nCurrent CSR code places H2D and GPU decode submission inside one\\n`serial_native.submit_decode()` call. Splitting the outer Python call into fake\\n“H2D duration” and “decode duration” labels would be misleading, so this patch\\ndoes not do that. Use the underlying GPU memcpy and decode-kernel records to\\nseparate the actual activities. Their layer is identified by the enclosing\\nCSR label. This patch does not provide a causal W-wait/KV-wait breakdown by\\ninventing timing events; absent proof, a blank interval remains a gap.\\n\\nColor/category: compute green; weight blue; KV transfer teal; CSR restore purple;\\nCPU preparation grey; CPU wait/GPU wait-registration red; encode brown; free\\norange. Layer numbers remain text, not color. These are NVTX colors, not a\\npromise to recolor every profiler CUDA activity record.\\n\\nCUDA stream names are requested through the optional legacy NVTX resource API if\\navailable. Shared handles get a combined role name, never separate fake streams.\\nIf CUDA 13 does not ship libnvToolsExt, the labels still work through Python\\nNVTX; `capture.json` and a mark retain the CUDA-handle/role map. Those handles are\\n**not** CUPTI/Nsight numeric stream IDs. No stream is moved or created for looks.\\n\\n## Results\\n\\nEach suite cell has:\\n\\n```text\\nnsys/\\n  trace.nsys-rep\\n  capture.json\\n  capture_forwards.csv\\n  capture_kv_layers.csv\\n  trigger.json\\n  nsys-version.txt\\n```\\n\\n`capture.json`: capture phase/index, actual token count, decode B when known,\\nmax sequence length, runtime mode, active load-candidate blocks, unload blocks,\\nper-forward bytes, optional host history lengths, warnings and resource mapping.\\n\\n`capture_forwards.csv`: scalar one-row-per-forward view, including guard rows.\\n`capture_kv_layers.csv`: per-layer bytes/counters only for that short window.\\n\\nHost workload data comes from the existing `prepare_tail_step(input_batch)` call\\nbefore its full-block-policy early return. It reads only host\\n`InputBatch.num_computed_tokens_cpu`; it never copies `seq_lens` or `block_table`\\nfrom CUDA. Missing/stale host data is labelled unavailable. In DECODE, use the\\nhistory only when `history_matches_decode_batch` is true. In mixed batches,\\ninput-batch row count is not relabelled as an exact decode batch.\\n\\nThe final cell check fails on a missing/incomplete report, forward count, or\\nbyte accounting. It warns when the selected window contains no decode, no KV\\nH2D, or no usable host-context data. It does not claim that a file's existence\\nproves GPU tracing correctness.\\n\\n## Bytes: distinguish garbage from total entry gaps\\n\\nThe existing repository accountant is retained with GPU timing off:\\n\\n- `kv_raw_bytes`: dense-equivalent size of the selected KV.\\n- `kv_payload_bytes`: active encoded payload (or raw payload on a raw route).\\n- `kv_h2d_bytes`: submitted memcpy bytes, **not physical-link protocol traffic**.\\n- `cd3_metadata_bytes`, `cd3_alignment_bytes`, `cd3_gap_bytes`.\\n- `cd3_csr_garbage_bytes`: retired CSR entries inside that gap, a **subset**.\\n- `cd3_active_entry_bytes`, `cd3_entry_wire_bytes`: cached-plan values added to\\n  the current CSR counter dictionary; no block-by-block rescan.\\n- `cd3_copy_descriptors`, `cd3_batch_calls`, plan builds/hits, storage/execution.\\n\\nTwo derived byte budgets are saved:\\n\\n```text\\nwire_if_entry_gaps_removed_bytes = kv_h2d_bytes - cd3_gap_bytes\\nwire_if_retired_garbage_removed_bytes = kv_h2d_bytes - cd3_csr_garbage_bytes\\n```\\n\\nThey preserve the current mandatory routing, padding and useful payload. Do not\\nsubtract gap and garbage together. These values are not an algorithm-independent\\nminimum and not a TPOT forecast. The first includes removing inactive live entry\\nranges as well as retired garbage. Their actual elimination can change copy\\ncount/planning cost and must not be assumed free.\\n\\n`transfer_groups` in the layer CSV and `transfers` in the original accountant\\nare native/accounting groups, not memcpy-call count. Use explicit CD3 counters\\nor actual CUDA records for call/descriptor statistics. Ratios across forwards\\nmust be calculated from byte sums, not averages of ratios. Separate DECODE and\\nPREFILL_OR_MIXED and condition on workload size before interpreting raw/CSR time\\ndifferences as compression effects.\\n\\n## Scope and execution limitations\\n\\nPython/shell syntax, scoped counter lifecycle, request triggering, balanced\\nannotations, preset arguments and conservative old-patch migration have CPU-only\\ntests in `tests/`. No real GH200/B200, CUDA copy/decode, nsys injection, or GPU\\nreport was executed in the patch-writing environment. The server's profiler\\nversion, NVTX install and patched-vLLM ABI remain runtime dependencies.\\n\\nRun the optional CPU tests without loading the model:\\n\\n```bash\\n.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s \\\"$PATCH/tests\\\" -v\\n```\\n\\nFor a rollback, use the *newly generated* backup's exact diff:\\n`git apply --reverse --check <backup>/applied.patch` before\\n`git apply --reverse <backup>/applied.patch`. If that check fails, stop instead\\nof overwriting unrelated later edits.\\n\\n## Primary reference sources\\n\\nRemote code read at the pinned commit: serving suite/client, `torch_hooks.py`,\\n`v1_cuda_graph_wrapper.py`, `dual_memory_loader/kv.py`,\\n`chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py`, `kv_load_metrics.py`,\\n`kv_offload_scheduler.py`. The installer validates remaining annotation targets\\nagainst the local source AST before writing.\\n\\nOfficial profiler/annotation documentation:\\n\\n- https://docs.nvidia.com/nsight-systems/UserGuide/index.html\\n- https://nvidia.github.io/NVTX/python/reference.html\\n\\nThe official guide distinguishes CPU NVTX scopes, GPU projection, graph-node\\ntracing, graph precapture, and capture-range-end=stop. Those distinctions are\\npreserved in the labels and reporting rather than converted into fake timings.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"b97f8d\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000012128,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":892,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"scripts/offline/run_performance_suite.sh\\\": \\\"1511a186af58bc7096dcdbd4055a34249622175653d6d1190bd8251352001989\\\",\\n  \\\"scripts/serving/client/azure_conv.sh\\\": \\\"917790d408efd32a399439079745a3563ec442b066416f25eec6f8c9e25bc950\\\",\\n  \\\"scripts/serving/run_experiment.sh\\\": \\\"eb561d44014122e67a2f86abe5a485ee6df362309dbe0458f59c3e9e9f0e8468\\\",\\n  \\\"scripts/serving/run_performance_suite.sh\\\": \\\"3c783d0f1ccb7b9ec7f7c34e4dcd28d32f14e46ca50404e1bc8d89eb6a2f6e1e\\\",\\n  \\\"tests/test_cd3_hybrid_storage.py\\\": \\\"ff472050f6ba94ebbe31caabd11b4f73c804fe08b399d912e463acc098255cdc\\\",\\n  \\\"tests/test_cd3_kv_pipeline.py\\\": \\\"501393b0fc078719012156d333fe2e52738cca5760ca48220c616cedcf63de1c\\\",\\n  \\\"tiered_serve/chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py\\\": \\\"c3dd7df8e0416848ffd4527f0b5811ac4a4eecc75641c717e0de94abca89e65e\\\",\\n  \\\"tiered_serve/chunk_delta3_kv_plan.py\\\": \\\"7626df25e1f54c2753eeb8f75003889c3baf1811f1b2bb7edbe47103723faac0\\\",\\n  \\\"tiered_serve/compression/cuda/chunk_delta3_hybrid.h\\\": \\\"d7775ffa40a1eb4c07f82a57d6818b123d5a2a82f6bab65308370304c8376d0c\\\",\\n  \\\"tiered_serve/kv_codec_spec.py\\\": \\\"48579bd13b46b94a4fc93bf784fa9789bd5080e9a6df43f51b5392d351bb4a2e\\\",\\n  \\\"tiered_serve/kv_load_metrics.py\\\": \\\"c541023303128bc24a67592f3538d6f6ee181eaa2c7b1c2c6dea29299d0bd187\\\",\\n  \\\"docs/KV_LOAD_METRICS.md\\\": \\\"9323a66619c6d6f60a58a3f21b0c6e28436db6586f0a5139611f27e728dfeaef\\\",\\n  \\\"docs/cd3-kv.md\\\": \\\"2be4f6da6f9aa6627e73ca971389cc82aded25b5153d4c7047ccd6e0c04c6a71\\\",\\n  \\\"docs/cd3-page16-implementation-ko.md\\\": \\\"5653ba253b1e4dc1778305f98435e1dc96fa57598cfdbd2b78d146851ad3ddff\\\"\\n}\\nbin\\nclean_up_GH.sh\\nexperiment-res